\subtree{
  \title{ICPC @ Hendrix}

  \p{On Saturday I hosted a competition site for the [International
     Collegiate Programming Contest](https://icpc.global/) at
     Hendrix. 11 teams (including two from Hendrix) competed, and I
     think everyone had fun.  (See [these previous weeknotes](00R6) for the reasons I decided to try hosting this year.)  The worst part was trying to make enough copies of the
     OS image in just a few days before the contest, since it took me
     a couple hours to copy each USB key, and quite a few of them turned out to be bad.  Next year I will try a different USB brand,
     and also see if I can find someone in IT who can help copy them.
  }
}

\subtree{
  \title{Piano corner}

  \p{As a teenager I really loved Romantic composers (\eg Chopin,
  Rachmaninoff, Brahms (though not Debussy)).  I also played Bach
  because my piano teacher made me—not that I disliked it, but it's
  just not what I would have chosen to play on my own.  As I've gotten
  older, however, Bach has grown on me a lot.  My love for Romantic
  composers is undiminished, but these days I can get lost in learning
  Bach pieces in a way I never did growing up.}

  \p{All that is just to say that this week I have become obsessed
  with learning Bach's [French Suite No. 6 in E major (BVW 817)](00R5).
  I had already previously learned No. 4 (E♭ major) and No. 5 (G
  major).  I don't really know what triggered it, exactly; I think I
  just happened to flip to it, and it just grabbed me.  So far I've
  got the Allemande down pretty well and starting to work on
  the Courante.}
}
